@startuml
title SATRA-RV — Contract, Counterfactual, and Test Validation
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
actor Developer
participant "SATRA-RV Service" as SATRA
participant "Candidate Workspace" as WS
participant "Counterfactual Mutator" as MUT
participant "Pytest Runner" as TEST
participant "Test Validator" as VALID
participant "Ollama Adapter" as GEN
database "Evidence Store" as STORE
Developer -> SATRA : validate supported application candidate
SATRA -> WS : prepare baseline and candidate snapshots
WS --> SATRA : InvoiceHub Python inputs
SATRA -> TEST : run trusted baseline, trusted candidate, ordinary candidate tests
TEST --> SATRA : execution results and security findings
SATRA -> MUT : clone baseline; bypass invoice ownership guard
MUT --> SATRA : counterfactual application
SATRA -> TEST : run independent security oracle on mutant
TEST --> SATRA : mutant result
SATRA -> SATRA : establish counterfactual feasibility from baseline pass + assertion kill
SATRA -> VALID : preflight candidate security test source
VALID --> SATRA : syntax / safety / locality result
alt candidate test passes preflight
  SATRA -> TEST : run on secure baseline, counterfactual, and baseline repeat
  TEST --> SATRA : three test outcomes
  SATRA -> SATRA : diagnose oracle strength and repeatability
else candidate test rejected by preflight
  SATRA -> SATRA : classify security test integrity as rejected
end
opt generated proposals returned by Ollama
  SATRA -> GEN : request contract-focused test candidates
  GEN --> SATRA : candidate test sources + rule IDs
  loop each generated proposal
    SATRA -> VALID : preflight syntax, safety, locality, and rule identity
    VALID --> SATRA : accepted / rejected
    opt accepted proposal with matching contract rule
      SATRA -> TEST : run on baseline, mutant, then baseline repeat
      TEST --> SATRA : generated-test validation outcomes
      SATRA -> SATRA : accept only if baseline passes twice and mutant is killed
      SATRA -> TEST : run accepted proposal on candidate
      TEST --> SATRA : candidate result
    end
  end
end
SATRA -> SATRA : classify ACCEPT / REJECT / INCONCLUSIVE
SATRA -> STORE : persist decision, oracle, and execution evidence
SATRA --> Developer : findings + reproducible test evidence
note right of SATRA
Counterfactual operator: replace can_access_invoice with return True.
Scope is bounded to supported InvoiceHub authentication, ownership,
admin, upload, and parameterized-login checks.
end note
@enduml
